00:10:15.660 --> 00:10:16.940
And he was like, yes.

266
00:10:17.120 --> 00:10:17.720
Oh, my gosh.

267
00:10:17.720 --> 00:10:18.580
This is a podcaSt.

268
00:10:18.980 --> 00:10:21.500
He said, my friend Jeff should listen to this.

269
00:10:21.640 --> 00:10:24.360
He said his friend Jeff knew a lot about podcasting.

270
00:10:24.480 --> 00:10:25.440
So I'm like, OK.

271
00:10:25.800 --> 00:10:32.180
So we email it to Jeff, not knowing that Jeff was Jeff Ulrich, one of the founders of Earwolf.

272
00:10:32.380 --> 00:10:35.180
He's like the Steve Jobs of podcasting, basically.

273
00:10:35.780 --> 00:10:37.520
So Jeff listened to it.

274
00:10:37.740 --> 00:10:38.640
He agreed.

275
00:10:38.880 --> 00:10:41.380
And he said, do you want to meet with some people?

276
00:10:41.840 --> 00:10:45.720
And he eventually introduced us to a lot of people in the podcasting world.

277
00:10:46.000 --> 00:10:47.300
You know what I remember?

278
00:10:47.540 --> 00:10:47.740
What?

279
00:10:48.320 --> 00:10:49.520
We went to his house.

280
00:10:49.800 --> 00:10:51.860
And we were talking about it with him.

281
00:10:52.420 --> 00:10:55.860
And you kept saying, but where do we plug in the microphones?

282
00:10:56.140 --> 00:10:58.240
I was like, how do you get the microphones for it?

283
00:10:58.300 --> 00:10:59.180
Where do you get the microphones?

284
00:10:59.180 --> 00:11:00.840
Because we recorded this on our iPhone.

285
00:11:01.000 --> 00:11:02.480
But like, we'll need regular microphones.

286
00:11:02.720 --> 00:11:06.060
You were so curious about the production from the very beginning.

287
00:11:06.060 --> 00:11:08.200
And he was like, I don't want to talk about the microphones.

288
00:11:08.400 --> 00:11:09.160
