289
00:11:09.320 --> 00:11:12.860
He's like, I'm talking about a vision for what this could be to you.

290
00:11:13.100 --> 00:11:14.240
And I'm like, yeah, I know.

291
00:11:14.360 --> 00:11:18.280
I guess I just am wondering, like, where do you upload it?

292
00:11:18.500 --> 00:11:20.560
Well, you always said, and I love this.

293
00:11:20.700 --> 00:11:23.060
You were like, don't be afraid to ask a lot of dumb questions.

294
00:11:23.220 --> 00:11:26.420
Because we were learning a whole new genre.

295
00:11:26.720 --> 00:11:28.620
This was an absolute big career pivot.

296
00:11:28.620 --> 00:11:29.880
And we didn't know what we were doing.

297
00:11:30.200 --> 00:11:30.480
Yeah.

298
00:11:30.620 --> 00:11:33.400
And we had the benefit of our name value, right?

299
00:11:33.540 --> 00:11:34.300
Like, that's something.

300
00:11:34.440 --> 00:11:35.220
And that is valuable.

301
00:11:35.220 --> 00:11:38.740
And we had our true life memories of working on this show

302
00:11:38.740 --> 00:11:40.700
and our friendships with the cast and crew.

303
00:11:40.860 --> 00:11:44.700
But otherwise, this was a whole new section of the entertainment industry.

304
00:11:44.820 --> 00:11:45.980
We didn't know anything about it.

305
00:11:46.200 --> 00:11:47.180
And so we did.

306
00:11:47.300 --> 00:11:48.080
We went out there.

307
00:11:48.220 --> 00:11:49.180
We made ourselves vulnerable.

308
00:11:49.400 --> 00:11:51.700
We asked a lot of dumb questions and a lot of meetings.

309
00:11:51.880 --> 00:11:55.400
But the more we looked at it, the more podcasting really made sense.

310
00:11:55.540 --> 00:11:57.460
Because it was a stable job in Los Angeles,

311
00:11:57.940 --> 00:12:00.640
