312
00:12:00.840 --> 00:12:02.800
We would be able to set our own schedules,

313
00:12:03.240 --> 00:12:05.060
which was very important to us.

314
00:12:05.220 --> 00:12:07.300
It was something we could do while our kids were at school.

315
00:12:07.640 --> 00:12:12.280
It just, it really seemed like it could open up a whole new lifestyle for us.

316
00:12:12.620 --> 00:12:16.800
And then, of course, best of all, we could work together again in a creative way.

317
00:12:16.960 --> 00:12:17.120
Yeah.

318
00:12:17.520 --> 00:12:19.860
It was best friendship and putting family firSt.

319
00:12:20.180 --> 00:12:21.440
And that's how we got here.

320
00:12:21.560 --> 00:12:25.700
And cleaning out our garages and sheds, which makes me say, lady,

321
00:12:25.700 --> 00:12:28.220
what could happen on the next big clean?

322
00:12:28.900 --> 00:12:29.800
I don't know.

323
00:12:30.720 --> 00:12:31.960
What's in there?

324
00:12:32.720 --> 00:12:36.680
You know, I hadn't listened to this recording since we did it.

325
00:12:36.880 --> 00:12:38.320
It's been seven years.

326
00:12:38.520 --> 00:12:38.700
Yeah.

